\newcommand{\arcoth}{\mathop{\rm arcoth}\nolimits}]

Content:
We can define the reciprocal hyperbolic functions similarly to how we define reciprocal trigonometric functions.

Content:
The hyperbolic cosecant function (pronounced "cosetch") is defined as
[MATH: \csch{x} = \dfrac{1}{\sinh{x}} = \dfrac{2}{e^x-e^{-x}}\,\,\, .]
The graph of [MATH: y=\csch x] is shown below.

Graphic:
[IMG: /graphics/a544b6842b8023fe6dc2a7243ab4aa8d]

Content:
Note the following properties of [MATH: y=\csch x\mathbin{:}]

Content:
- Its domain is [MATH: x \in (-\infty, 0)\cup (0,\infty).]
- Its range is [MATH: y \in (-\infty, 0)\cup (0,\infty).]
- It is an odd function.

