Content:
The hyperbolic secant function (pronounced "sesh") is defined as
[MATH: \sech{x} = \dfrac{1}{\cosh{x}} = \dfrac{2}{e^x+e^{-x}}\,\,\, .]
The graph of [MATH: y=\sech x] is shown below.

Graphic:
[IMG: /graphics/2297f59763224e98dc496bf5e3625dd1]

Content:
Note the following properties of [MATH: y=\sech x\mathbin{:}]

Content:
- Its domain is [MATH: x \in (-\infty, \infty).]
- Its range is [MATH: y \in (0, 1].]
- It has the horizontal asymptote [MATH: y=0.]
- It is an even function.

