The definition of [MATH: \coth x] is
[MATH: \coth x|= (1)/(	anh x); = (e^{x} + e^{− x})/(e^{x} − e^{− x}); = (e^{2x} + 1)/(e^{2x} − 1); = (1 + e^{− 2x})/(1 − e^{− 2x}).]

Using the fourth definition, we get

[MATH: \coth (− \ln 3)|= (1 + e^{− 2(− \ln 3)})/(1 − e^{− 2(− \ln 3)}); = (1 + e^{2\ln 3})/(1 − e^{2\ln 3}); = (1 + e^{\ln 3^{2}})/(1 − e^{\ln 3^{2}}); = (1 + 3^{2})/(1 − 3^{2}); = (1 + 9)/(1 − 9); = (10)/((− 8)); = − (5)/(4).]

